==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|hvat|lang=is}}, originally the neuter form of {{m|non|*hver}} (from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*hwaz}}), but conflated with {{term|hverr|lang=non}} (whence Modern Icelandic {{term|hver|lang=is}}). Corresponds to {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*hwat}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*kʷód}}, {{m|ine-pro|*kʷod}}. See {{term|hver|lang=is}}.

